Package: pawh
Title: Computational Toolkit for Heterogeneity in Statistical Genetics
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Akil", family = "Anthony", email = "akilanthony19@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides analytic power and minimum sample size necessary (MSSN)
    calculations for genetic association study designs described in Gordon et
    al. (2020), "Heterogeneity in Statistical Genetics". Public interfaces
    cover case-control genotype chi-square and trend tests, family-based
    transmission disequilibrium tests (TDT), and single- and multivariate
    quantitative-trait designs using ANOVA, threshold-selected genotype
    chi-square tests, and Pillai MANOVA. Methods can account for locus
    heterogeneity and supported phenotype or genotype misclassification
    mechanisms. Functions return structured results and include static and
    interactive visualizations for study design, teaching, and methodological
    validation.
